            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0547" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.94/644</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State (Phillips) to the
                        Ambassador in Japan (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-31">October 31, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Grew</hi>: I acknowledge receipt of your
                    confidential letter of October 6 giving a review of factors in the
                    Russo-Japanese situation and an estimate of possibilities. We have found this
                    material very useful and are very glad to have your views. Your estimate and
                    ours are in accord. I am sure that you will continue to watch this situation
                    closely and we will of course count on you to inform us of any developments of
                    importance in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
